    "The species: Malus x micromalus Makino, xifu haitang: a small tree 2.5-5 m, upright, the branches ascending; leaves elliptic to oblong-elliptic 5-10 cm by 2.5-5 cm; flowers pink in April to May; fruit subglobose 1-1.5 cm, red, ripe in September (Flora of China (Wu Zhengyi, P. H. Raven and Hong Deyuan, eds., Science Press and Missouri Botanical Garden, 1994-2013), vol. 9, Rosaceae).",
    "Habit: the as-built museum's tree grower (windows/Source/MuseeVision/Nature/MuseeTree.cpp, OrchardSpec (apple) for the court's crabapples, 4.6 m, crown at 3.3 m, radii 1.7 and 1.2, which this record steepens to the xifu haitang's upright, vase-like habit), its branching, leaf and crown numbers.",
    "Colours: the as-built apple's summer greens."
